ve here in `/srv/git/3tched-container`.\n   * The core D-Bus backend services and plugins reside in `/srv/git/odbus-verified`.\n   * The user-facing dashboard lives in `/srv/git/3tched.com`.\n\n2. **Nested Btrfs Avoidance**:\n   * The container rootfs runs on Incus `identity-roots` (`dir` driver pool) rather than native host Btrfs subvolumes, avoiding the `op-storage-kernel-guard` nested Btrfs ioctl deny rules.\n   * Writable rootfs capacity is provided by attaching a discrete per-container image (`make-cozo-device.sh`) and running `btrfs device add` **inside the container**.\n\n3. **Dedicated Ext4 Partition for Cozo / RocksDB**:\n   * To prevent Write-Ahead Log (WAL) and SST compaction fragmentation on Copy-on-Write Btrfs, Cozo's persistent store is backed by a dedicated **ext4** partition (`p2` of the attached image).\n   * RocksDB writes in pure allocate-on-write mode (`allow_fallocate = false`), keeping sparse images compact without un-sparsifying disk allocations.\n\n## Directory Structure\n\n```\n/srv/git/3tched-container/\n├── instances/\n│   └── chatbot-template.json       # Pure JSON instance specification (config, devices, profiles)\n├── profiles/\n│   └── 3tched-lungs.json           # JSON profile defining the /run/opdbus/lungs socket & fuse\n├── storage/\n│   └── make-cozo-device.sh         # Creates pre-formatted 20G image (10G Btrfs leaf + 10G ext4 Cozo)\n├── scripts/\n│   └── launch-identity.sh          # JSON-driven launcher: injects UUID/keys and boots\n└── README.md\n```\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### 1. Pre-format a Cozo Storage Device\n```bash\nsudo ./storage/make-cozo-device.sh /var/lib/op-dbus/identity-cozo/devices/id-1.img 20\n```\n\n### 2. Launch an Identity Container\n```bash\nsudo ./scripts/launch-identity.sh id-1 '<wireguard_public_key>'\n```\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"/srv/git/3tched-container/README.md"}}]}
