{"step_index":1855,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T13:34:22Z","input_tokens":2402,"cache_read_tokens":217455,"output_tokens":2735,"thinking":"A tool is available to create a structured pitch deck document. The deck will reside within a designated directory and file path, organized slide-by-slide. The initial slides will outline the title/hook and the problem being addressed.\n\n\nThe market analysis points to significant investment in fractional real estate, but existing platforms rely on centralized intermediaries. The proposed solution leverages sovereign AI agents within containerized environments for compliant real estate transactions. This involves establishing cryptographic identities, utilizing open-weight models for intelligent processing, and implementing secure storage with Ethereum smart contract integration.\n\nThe system's architecture will encompass cryptographic identity, open-weight models structured by a taxonomy, a storage solution, and secure settlement through Ethereum. This framework allows for peer-to-peer protocol fees instead of conventional brokerage fees, providing a competitive edge due to container isolation and OSCAL compliance. I will now structure the pitch deck around these core elements.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Comprehensive 10-slide pitch deck for the $250k hackathon: Sovereign AI Agents, OSCAL Compliance Routing, and Ethereum Smart Contract Settlement for Decentralized Real Estate.","UserFacing":true},"Content":"# 3tchedFS: Sovereign Agents & OSCAL-Compliant Smart Contract Settlement\n\n> **The Decentralized Protocol Disrupting the $50 Trillion Real Estate Cartel**  \n> *Sovereign Containerized AI Identities • OSCAL Compliance Routing • Atomic Ethereum Settlement*\n\n---\n\n## Slide 1: The Title & Hook\n* **Title**: **3tchedFS Protocol**\n* **Tagline**: Sovereign AI Agents Executing Compliant Real Estate Settlement on Ethereum\n* **The One-Liner**: Replacing centralized real estate monopolies (MLS, title cartels, opaque escrow) with sovereign containerized AI agents and verifiable, OSCAL-compliant smart contracts.\n* **Target Prize**: $250,000 Hackathon Grand Prize\n\n---\n\n## Slide 2: The Problem — The $50T Cartel Bottleneck\n1. **Centralized Listing Monopolies (MLS / CoStar / Zillow)**:\n   * Private walled gardens gatekeeping property data and charging predatory access tolls.\n   * Single points of failure currently facing massive antitrust scrutiny.\n2. **Opaque & Archaic Closing Middlemen**:\n   * Weeks of manual due diligence across title companies, escrow officers, underwriters, and county clerks.\n   * **6% to 10% fee drag** on every transaction for routine administrative verification.\n3. **The Web3 Failure**:\n   * Prior \"crypto real estate\" projects failed because smart contracts operate in a regulatory vacuum—they cannot parse zoning laws, title liens, or regulatory compliance without human oracles.\n\n---\n\n## Slide 3: The Market Tailwinds — The \"Bezos / Arrived\" Opportunity\n* **The Trend**: Jeff Bezos (Bezos Expeditions) and major VC funds are pouring hundreds of millions into fractional real estate platforms like **Arrived**.\n* **The Validation**: Millions of retail investors want liquid, fractional real estate with instant yields.\n* **The Flaw**: Platforms like Arrived recreate the exact same centralized middlemen, charging 8%+ platform fees, holding assets on closed private ledgers, and gatekeeping listing selection.\n* **The Opportunity**: **A truly decentralized, P2P protocol** where buyers and sellers transact directly through sovereign agent representatives, cutting transaction overhead from weeks and 6% down to seconds and cents.\n\n---\n\n## Slide 4: The Solution — 3tchedFS\nA full-stack, hardware-isolated agent architecture combining **system container identities**, **standardized OSCAL compliance taxonomy**, and **Ethereum smart contracts**:\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph Discovery [\"1. Decentralized Discovery\"]\n        A[\"Buyer Agent (Incus Container)\"] -->|\"Semantic Query\"| B[(\"Cozo Graph + Qdrant Vectors\")]\n        C[\"Seller Agent (Incus Container)\"] -->|\"P2P Listing Publish\"| B\n    end\n\n    subgraph Compliance [\"2. OSCAL Compliance Engine\"]\n        A -->|\"Subcategory Taxonomy (mut.* / obs.*)\"| D{\"OSCAL Compliance Gate\"}\n        D -->|\"NIST 800-53 Checks\"| E[\"Title & Lien Attestation\"]\n        D -->|\"Meta/Llama Open Weights\"| F[\"Regulatory Policy Validation\"]\n        D -->|\"2-of-N Cryptographic Gate\"| G[\"Dual Superadmin WireGuard Keys\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Settlement [\"3. Ethereum Smart Contract\"]\n        E & F & G -->|\"Attestation Digest & Proofs\"| H[\"Ethereum Escrow / Title Contract\"]\n        H -->|\"Atomic Execution\"| I[\"Deed & Tokenized Share Transfer\"]\n        H -->|\"Instant Settlement\"| J[\"Funds / Rent Escrow Release\"]\n    end\n```\n\n---\n\n## Slide 5: The Secret Sauce — Ground-Up Architecture\nUnlike flimsy chatbot wrappers, 3tchedFS is engineered from bare-metal systems constraints:\n\n1. **The Container IS the Identity**:\n   * Each agent is an isolated Incus system container with its own PID/mount namespaces, seccomp filters, and cryptographic WireGuard identity (`Env5z...`).\n   * Zero unconfined host execution rights; operating strictly via delegated capabilities.\n2. **OSCAL Subcategory Taxonomy Plugin**:\n   * Every operation carries a typed subcategory (`obs.legal.title@v1`, `mut.escrow.deposit@v1`).\n   * Universal compliance inheritance across all 74 plugins automatically via `ensure_category_metadata_fields`.\n3. **Optimized Storage Substrate**:\n   * Immutable Btrfs seed baseline paired with a writable sprout leaf.\n   * **Dedicated ext4 slice for Cozo / RocksDB**: Prevents Btrfs Copy-on-Write fragmentation and write amplification, keeping sparse disk footprints minimal.\n\n---\n\n## Slide 6: How It Works — A Real-World Transaction Flow\n\n| Step | Action | Execution Layer | Cryptographic Verification |\n| :---: | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **1** | **Discovery** | Buyer agent discovers property via semantic vector memory | In-process Cozo Datalog + Qdrant |\n| **2** | **Due Diligence** | Agent verifies title, zoning, and encumbrances | OSCAL `obs.property.title@v1` receipt |\n| **3** | **Dual Sign-Off** | High-value settlement approved | 2-of-N WireGuard superadmin signatures |\n| **4** | **Escrow Deposit** | Buyer agent deposits earnest funds | Ethereum smart contract locks funds |\n| **5** | **Atomic Settlement** | Deeds/fractional shares transfer; funds release | Smart contract executes on-chain state change |\n| **6** | **Audit Finality** | Transaction hash anchored to local Snowball chain | Permanent tamper-proof audit trail |\n\n---\n\n## Slide 7: Business Model & Unit Economics\n* **Protocol Fee (0.25% - 0.50%)**:\n  * Massive savings compared to traditional 5% - 6% broker commissions.\n  * On a $500,000 property: **$1,250 protocol fee vs. $30,000 legacy fee**.\n* **Identity Sled Licensing & Enterprise Compliance Feeds**:\n  * Institutional property managers and funds pay recurring fees for enterprise NIST 800-53 / SOC2 automated audit attestations.\n* **Gas-Optimized Rollup Economics**:\n  * Local Snowball hash chains aggregate hundreds of agent turns and due diligence steps off-chain, committing only the single Merkle state root to Ethereum to minimize gas fees.\n\n---\n\n## Slide 8: Competitive Matrix\n\n| Capability | Legacy Real Estate (MLS / Title) | PropTech (Arrived / Roofstock) | Standard Web3 AI (Wrappers) | **3tchedFS Protocol** |\n| :--- | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| **Decentralized Listings** | ❌ Walled garden | ❌ Walled garden | ⚠️ Raw IPFS | **✅ P2P Agent Mesh** |\n| **Regulatory Compliance** | ⚠️ Manual lawyers | ⚠️ Manual legal team | ❌ None | **✅ Automated OSCAL Taxonomy** |\n| **Identity Isolation** | ❌ N/A | ❌ Corporate accounts | ❌ API keys in plaintext | **✅ Incus Containers + WireGuard** |\n| **Closing Speed** | 30–60 Days | 7–14 Days | N/A | **Under 60 Seconds** |\n| **Transaction Fees** | 6% – 10% | 8%+ embedded drag | Gas only | **0.25% – 0.50%** |\n\n---\n\n## Slide 9: Live Hackathon Demo Walkthrough\n1. **Container Launch**: Instantiate a sovereign buyer agent from the modular `/srv/git/3tched-container` template.\n2. **P2P Memory Search**: The buyer agent queries the seller agent's property catalog using semantic retrieval across Cozo and Qdrant.\n3. **OSCAL Compliance Check**: The compliance engine triggers an automated policy verification using open-weight Meta models and signs the receipt.\n4. **2-of-N WireGuard Dual-Signature**: Two registered admin keys sign the transaction payload.\n5. **On-Chain Settlement**: The Ethereum smart contract validates the compliance proof and executes atomic escrow release live on Sepolia/Arbitrum.\n\n---\n\n## Slide 10: 10-Day Sprint Roadmap & Vision\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    A[\"Day 1-3: Core Verification<br>• Cozo + Qdrant memory loop<br>• OSCAL subcategory validation\"] --> B[\"Day 4-6: Multi-Sig & Delegation<br>• 2-of-N WireGuard approvals<br>• Containerized agent dispatch\"]\n    B --> C[\"Day 7-8: Ethereum Contracts<br>• Escrow & settlement contract<br>• Attestation verification\"]\n    C --> D[\"Day 9-10: Demo & Submission<br>• Svelte UI integration<br>• Live video walkthrough<br>• $250k Prize Submission\"]\n```\n\n* **The Long-Term Vision**: The global standard for autonomous, legally compliant commerce between sovereign artificial intelligences.\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"/home/jeremy/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/952bc719-abd2-42eb-a14d-385b181c96ff/pitch_deck.md"}}]}
